## Data Model

The application uses three C structures:

- `Car` stores vehicle specifications and stock status.
- `Customer` stores contact details for a recorded buyer.
- `Sale` links a vehicle and customer to a dated transaction and sale price.

The current implementation uses bounded in-memory arrays and pipe-delimited local data files. IDs are assigned sequentially and sales retain their own transaction records when a vehicle is archived.

## Technical Concepts

- C structures and arrays
- Pointers and passing structures to functions
- String handling and case-insensitive searching
- Sorting and aggregation
- Input validation and defensive programming
- File I/O and persistence
- Date/time handling with the C standard library
- Modular function design

## Limitations

AutoLot Pro is an educational, single-user terminal application. It is not a production dealership platform.

It does not process payments, provide authentication, encrypt customer data, support concurrent users or implement accounting-grade data integrity.

Customer details are stored locally in plain text. Use synthetic data only.

